> Shouldn't stone giants be banned from Sobokan?

I don't think so; they make a (Sokoban-) game more interesting.

Part of the fun with Nethack is that once you think you can rely on
something a monster appears that nullifies your feeling of security.

For example you'll notice that...
- you secure yourself by locked doors; they may be unlocked e.g. by
   shopkeepers and riders, passed by amorphous creatures and ghosts,
   kicked down by giants
- you are safe in a room without (detected) doors; dwarfs will dig
   through the walls, rockmoles and umber hulks eat walls and create
   corridors, some high level spellcasting monsters teleport to you
- you are sure you can handle every creature of a certain difficulty
   level, then shapechangers will pop in and kill you in a high level
   form
- you think boulders are a fortress until giants appear or soldiers
   zap wands of striking
- you collected valuable items and gold, but leprechauns, nymphs,
   and monkeys don't respect any private property
- you drop your spare loot at the bottom, just to notice monsters
   pick them up and use it, gelatineous cubes or xorns to eat it
- engrave protecting words to save yourself and dropped objects,
   but quite some monsters don't respect that engraving
- ...and much more

This all are not only balancing factors but it also keeps the game
interesting during your characters life.

